WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.460
Every car sits in a column for its stage:

00:00:02.460 --> 00:00:05.130
checked in, diagnosing, estimate review,

00:00:05.130 --> 00:00:07.140
waiting on parts, in progress,

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:09.630
quality check, and ready for pickup.

00:00:09.630 --> 00:00:13.224
On a phone, the columns become one simple list.

00:00:13.224 --> 00:00:15.024
Let's check in a new car.

00:00:15.024 --> 00:00:19.554
Sam Ortiz just dropped off his 2014 Mazda CX-5.

00:00:19.554 --> 00:00:22.434
We enter his name, and choose how to notify him:

00:00:22.434 --> 00:00:24.864
by text, by email, or both.

00:00:24.864 --> 00:00:26.664
Sam wants both.

00:00:26.664 --> 00:00:28.764
Then his cell number and email,

00:00:28.764 --> 00:00:31.104
the vehicle, and what he's hearing:

00:00:31.104 --> 00:00:33.894
a squealing belt on cold starts.

00:00:33.894 --> 00:00:37.764
This box confirms Sam agreed to receive updates.

00:00:37.764 --> 00:00:40.080
Then we check him in.

00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:40.980
And that's it.

00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:43.470
Sam was just notified that we have his car,

00:00:43.470 --> 00:00:45.120
with a link to follow along.

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:47.250
That link is his own page for this car.

00:00:47.250 --> 00:00:49.440
No app, and no password.

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:52.320
Every notification shows up here in the message thread,

00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:55.350
marked text or email, so the whole team can see what

00:00:55.350 --> 00:00:57.168
was sent and when.

00:00:57.168 --> 00:00:59.458
Now let's look at a car that's further along.

00:00:59.458 --> 00:01:03.168
Lena's Chevy Malibu came in with the AC blowing warm.

00:01:03.168 --> 00:01:04.488
The tech found the problem,

00:01:04.488 --> 00:01:06.288
so we'll build an estimate.

00:01:06.288 --> 00:01:10.008
As we type, Talk Shops suggests items the shop has saved,

00:01:10.008 --> 00:01:11.328
with their prices.

00:01:11.328 --> 00:01:13.308
We pick the AC recharge,

00:01:13.308 --> 00:01:15.138
for 189 dollars.

00:01:15.138 --> 00:01:17.598
Then the condenser, for 624.

00:01:17.598 --> 00:01:21.744
Anything new can be saved for next time with one checkbox.

00:01:21.744 --> 00:01:23.154
When the estimate is ready,

00:01:23.154 --> 00:01:24.714
we send it for approval.

00:01:24.714 --> 00:01:27.234
Talk Shops writes the message for you,

00:01:27.234 --> 00:01:29.514
with the total and the customer's link.

00:01:29.514 --> 00:01:31.494
You can change the wording if you like.

00:01:31.494 --> 00:01:33.192
Then we send it.

00:01:33.192 --> 00:01:34.012
No problem.

00:01:34.012 --> 00:01:36.612
Here's what Lena sees when she opens the link on her

00:01:36.612 --> 00:01:37.302
phone.

00:01:37.302 --> 00:01:39.312
Her car, where it's at in the process,

00:01:39.312 --> 00:01:40.272
and the estimate.

00:01:40.272 --> 00:01:43.422
She can approve or decline each repair on its own.

00:01:43.422 --> 00:01:45.492
Let's say she approves the recharge,

00:01:45.492 --> 00:01:47.682
but holds off on the condenser for now.

00:01:47.682 --> 00:01:49.422
She types her name to sign,

00:01:49.422 --> 00:01:50.892
and sends her decision.

00:01:50.892 --> 00:01:54.222
And every customer page links to the privacy policy at the

00:01:54.222 --> 00:01:55.584
bottom.

00:01:56.884 --> 00:01:59.974
Back at the shop, her answer shows up right away.

00:01:59.974 --> 00:02:02.164
You can see exactly what she approved,

00:02:02.164 --> 00:02:04.036
and her signature with the time.

00:02:04.036 --> 00:02:07.546
From here, you move the car along as the work happens.

00:02:07.546 --> 00:02:08.656
In progress.

00:02:08.656 --> 00:02:09.946
Quality check.

00:02:09.946 --> 00:02:11.866
Each step can notify the customer,

00:02:11.866 --> 00:02:13.786
and you decide which ones go out.

00:02:13.786 --> 00:02:16.426
And when it's done, ready for pickup.

00:02:16.426 --> 00:02:20.644
The customer is notified with the total and your hours.
